Question #10

Run class() on student["grades"] and student[["grades"]] and explain the difference between [ ] and [[ ]].

ANSWER: student["grades"] has class "list" and student[["grades"]] has class "numeric". Single brackets return a smaller list (the container with the item still inside), while double brackets return the actual item stored inside.

Question #11

Why does R distinguish between [ ] and [[ ]] for lists, but a vector only needs [ ]?

ANSWER: A vector holds only single values of one type, so [ ] is enough. A list can hold different types and even other vectors or lists, so R needs [ ] to get a sub-list and [[ ]] to pull out the actual element.


